<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zababa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zababa was a Mesopotamian god of war and the patron deity of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kish">Kish</a>. His temple there was called E-mete-ursag, and his consort was the goddess Bau or, in later times, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inanna">Inanna</a>, who also had a temple at Kish. He was later identified with Ninurta and other warrior gods, and the name appears in royal names such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur-zababa">Ur-Zababa</a>, the king of Kish whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a> served.</p></div>
